{
  "$comment": "The never-break-the-host rule as cases. Each SDK runs every case that applies to it against its public API and asserts that every step returned, that nothing was thrown or rejected (including asynchronously, until the client has closed), and that no warning, notice or deprecation was raised on a host that treats them as fatal.",
  "version": 1,
  "$notes": {
    "capability": "As in scenarios.json: common, backend, browser. A step may carry its own `capability`, and `js` means the JavaScript SDKs. A step naming a method the SDK does not have is skipped; a case with no runnable step is skipped.",
    "hostile": "`hostile(kind)` anywhere in args or options is replaced by the SDK's own rendering of that kind (see `kinds`). Where a language has no such value, use the nearest one it has. `error(message)` is a new Error; `rejected(handled)` is a promise that rejects and whose rejection the test has already handled.",
    "steps": "Every step must return without throwing, whatever it returns. `withScope` and `enterScope` with nested `steps` run them in the callback; with `args` the argument stands in for the callback. `scope` runs its steps on the scope object the client hands out. `withinMs` bounds how long the call may block. `request` and `requestThatThrows` go through each framework adapter the SDK ships.",
    "options": "Merged over the test's default options. `$runtime` names a condition the test arranges before constructing the client: frozenGlobals (every global the SDK patches is frozen or non-writable), unreachableHost (every send hangs until its deadline). hooks/logger/onError/transport set to `throws` or `allThrow` are callbacks that throw every time they are called.",
    "host": "Host functions to exercise after the steps, through whatever the SDK wrapped them with, comparing against the unwrapped behaviour: same return, same error, same synchronous-or-asynchronous failure, the original called exactly once. `fetch(invalid)` and `xhr(invalid)` call them with arguments the platform itself rejects or coerces. `errorHandler(levels)` installs a host error handler for one level before the SDK and asserts it is never called for another.",
    "expect": "As in scenarios.json, plus `logged: {level, count}`: exactly that many lines at that level reached the configured logger."
  },
  "kinds": {
    "cycle": "A plain object/array that contains itself two levels down.",
    "throwing_accessor": "Reading or serialising it throws: a getter or Proxy trap that throws (JS); an object whose __toString and jsonSerialize throw (PHP).",
    "self_replicating": "Its serialiser returns a fresh value with the same serialiser, forever: toJSON returning a new object with toJSON (JS); jsonSerialize returning new self (PHP).",
    "no_json_form": "BigInt, NaN and Infinity, a symbol, a function (JS); NAN and INF, a closure, a resource (PHP), together in one object.",
    "deep": "Plain nesting 20,000 levels deep.",
    "huge": "A 5 MB string.",
    "bad_text": "A string that is not valid Unicode: a lone surrogate (JS), invalid UTF-8 bytes (PHP).",
    "null": "null / undefined.",
    "integer": "The integer 42 where a string is expected.",
    "object": "An empty plain object where a string or callable is expected.",
    "list_of_null": "A list whose only element is null, where a list of patterns or strings is expected."
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "cycle as data, everywhere data is accepted",
      "capability": "common",
      "steps": [
        {
          "do": "track",
          "args": [
            "checkout_completed",
            {
              "v": "hostile(cycle)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "identify",
          "args": [
            "user_1",
            {
              "v": "hostile(cycle)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "register",
          "args": [
            {
              "v": "hostile(cycle)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "setContext",
          "args": [
            "cart",
            {
              "v": "hostile(cycle)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "setTag",
          "args": [
            "plan",
            "hostile(cycle)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "addBreadcrumb",
          "args": [
            {
              "message": "step",
              "data": {
                "v": "hostile(cycle)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "captureMessage",
          "args": [
            "after hostile scope"
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "captureException",
          "args": [
            "error(boom)",
            {
              "context": {
                "v": "hostile(cycle)"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "withScope",
          "steps": [
            {
              "do": "track",
              "args": [
                "inside_scope"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "flush"
        }
      ]
    },
